  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Somning Shivanna Pujari vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 April, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 2023:Bhc-As:10636 P.H. Jayani 27(B)Aba3234.20 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 3234 Of 2022 Somning Shivanna Pujari ... Appl v/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Res Mr. Veerdhaval Kakade for the Applicant. Mr. S.V. Gavand, App for the State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 06th April, 2023. P. C. :- . This is an Application under section 438 of Cr.P.C. filed by the aforesaid Applicant apprehending his arrest in C.R.No.692/2022 registered with Pandharpur City Police Station, Solapur Rural for offences punishable under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code and sections 3, 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e) and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "3. It is the case of the prosecution that on 07/10/2022, the vehicle bearing No. MH-09-CA-3630 was intercepted and gutkha, pan masala P.H. Jayani 27(B)ABA3234.2022.doc and scented tobacco which are prohibited items, were seized from the said vehicle. The vehicle is owned by the Applicant and hence, crime came to be registered against the Applicant for committing the aforesaid offences. Learned APP states that the Applicant has reported to the Investigating Officer and that he has been investigated. Learned APP, under instructions, states that the presence of the Somning Shivanna Pujari vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/148437229/ 1 Applicant is not required for the purpose of custodial interrogation.",
